            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. The change adds a pure Stop-event decoder and encoder: DecodeStop reuses decodeEnvelope, which enforces the size bound and rejects malformed input, and StopReply.Encode returns no output for an allow and a block with a fallback reason when none is given. Neither function does I/O, retries, or holds state, so no concrete failure mode, rollback hazard, latency, or load impact is introduced.",
              "The stop_hook_active flag is decoded and exposed as Stop.Continuing, so a caller can avoid an endless block loop. The loop-prevention policy is not part of this candidate, so no finding is raised here.",
              "Decode errors on wrong-typed fields are returned as errors rather than ignored, and the tests in engine/hookwire/stop_test.go cover the oversize, wrong-type, relative-cwd and fallback-reason paths.",
              "The edit to engine/hookwire/boundary_test.go only adds stop_hook_active to the protocol tag list and has no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
