              "Reviewed all four changed paths from the provided patches. DecodeStop reuses decodeEnvelope and cleanCwd, which are not visible in the candidate; I take their size bound, single-object and wrong-type error behavior from the stop_test.go cases and the DecodeStop doc comment, not from their source.",
              "stop_test.go checks the observable behavior: field extraction, a relative cwd read as missing, wrong-type errors, non-object and two-object input, the ErrTooLarge bound, the exact block JSON with \u003c, \u003e and \u0026 kept unescaped, the fallback reason, and no output for a non-blocking reply.",
              "StopReply.Encode returns nil output when Block is false, and the test asserts this. Reason is ignored without a block, which is documented and tested, so no option is silently dropped.",
